# Stage 1: example B1 with a pi- beam, everything P9-P13 owes inactivated,
# and Decay and hadElastic LEFT ACTIVE.
#
# One line more than pi+: `hBertiniCaptureAtRest`. See muon_minus for what that switch
# means on both sides. Nothing stops here anyway (779.3 mm of range against 300 mm), so
# what the line buys is that the comparison is not resting on a process that cannot fire
# being left active - which is a different claim from it not mattering.
#
# Every name below is a row of ref/oracle/species_processes.csv for pi- - the dump of
# the constructed QBBC's own process manager. /process/inactivate ignores a name the
# species does not have, silently, so a macro written from the source rather than from
# the object can look like it switched something off. docs/RISK.md V43.

/run/initialize
/control/verbose 0
/run/verbose 1

/process/inactivate hBrems
/process/inactivate hPairProd
/process/inactivate pi-Inelastic
/process/inactivate hBertiniCaptureAtRest

# The stage, recorded by what RAN and not by what was intended. docs/RISK.md V43's
# lesson: ask the object. This prints Active/InActive for every process on the
# particle's manager, after the inactivations above.
/particle/select pi-
/particle/process/dump

/gun/particle pi-
/gun/energy 200 MeV

/run/printProgress 100000
/run/beamOn 500000
